      "text": "Inventurus Knowledge Solutions Limited Registered Address: 801, Building No. 5, 8th Floor, Mindspace Business Park (SEZ), Thane-Belapur Road, Airoli, Navi Mumbai – 400708, Thane, Maharashtra, India Ph.: +91 22 3071 1100 | W: www.ikshealth.com | CIN: L72200MH2006PLC337651 August 5, 2026 BSE Limited The Listing Department Phiroze Jeejeebhoy Towers 25th Floor, Dalal Street Fort, Mumbai 400 001 Maharashtra, India BSE Scrip Code: 544309 National Stock Exchange of India Limited The Listing Department Exchange Plaza, Plot No. C/1, G Block, Bandra Kurla Complex Bandra (East), Mumbai 400051 Maharashtra, India NSE Symbol: IKS Dear Sir/Ma’am, Sub: Investor Presentation Pursuant to Regulation 30 of the SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015, please find attached herewith investor presentation on the financial results of the Company for the quarter ended June 30, 2026. The said presentation is also being uploaded on the website of the Company at th e https://ikshealth.com/investor-relations/ Request you to take it on record and disseminate the same on your website. Thanking you. Yours sincerely, For Inventurus Knowledge Solutions Limited Sameer Chavan Company Secretary and Compliance Officer Membership No. F7211 Encl: As above 1 IKS Health Q1 FY 27 Investor Presentation 2 Disclaimer This presentation may include opinions and assumptions about future performance which could be considered as forward-looking statements. Forward-looking statements intrinsically cover several risks and uncertainties, which may lead to a material difference between actual results and the statements themselves. Such statements comprise the company’s current visibility on market movements, client discussions, and related factors. Inventurus Knowledge Solutions Limited does not assume an obligation to update or revise any forward-looking statements. 3 600+/650+ Healthcare Organizations Q1 27/Q1 26 12,889 / 1,902 Employees / Clinically trained staff (As of June 30, 2026) US$260bn / US$34bn TAM / Outsourced Market (CY2023) 8% / 12% TAM / Outsourced Market CAGR (2023-2028E) 85%+ Revenues from Repeat Customers 5+ Years Top 10 / Top 5 Clients Average Vintage (As of Mar 31, 2026) 565 Technology Focused Employees (As of June 30, 2026) 57 Sales & Marketing Employees (As of June 30, 2026) US$5tn US Healthcare Expenditure (CY2024) Total Addressable Market1,2 Established Client Relationships Specialised workforce The only Comprehensive platform that delegates all chores across the patient journey Adding a technology-enabled layer to ‘care delivery pyramid’ to help Physician Enterprises achieve optimized revenue and reduced expenses Note: Numbers Rounded off to nearest Integer / percent; 1. Source: Zinnov Report; 2. TAMTotal Addressable Market for RCM, VBC, Patient, Coding and Client Services. 3. Repeat clients refers to clients who availed our platform or solutions during the previous period, and revenue generated from such clients are calculated for the relevant period 3 IKS Health - a comprehensive healthcare enablement platform empowering provider organizations IKS Health: 5 strategic pillars of execution 4 Proprietary models driven comprehensive System of Action with API integration for large medical group market Integrated System of Action (SOA) & System of Record (SOR) for rural/ community health system market Drive growth momentum through re-stratified key growth levers Get back to optimized margins through operating model transformation and synergies Culture and leadership ●Create the structured uniﬁed data moat for AI training (5MM+ longitudinal records) that enable our SLM’s ●Train our proprietary SLM’s that power the interconnected workﬂows leveraging the above AI Training moat ●Build explainability in each of the Generative AI driven workﬂows; and empower with human-in-the-loop (HITL) and/or Rules-based AI for deterministic outcomes ●Embed the SOA agentic workﬂows in the native SOR (Electronic Health Record - EHR) workﬂows ●Translate the trained agentic workﬂows from Rural/ Community settings to the large group and ambulatory settings and vice versa ●Build API-powered integration with relevant EHRs ●Embody Explainability for Generative AI and HITL where applicable ●Continue to pursue feature-based KLAS leadership while demonstrating interconnected end to end agentic workﬂows (platform capabilities) ●Pick up land and expand (cross sell) momentum in installed base of Large Health Systems ●Cross sell System of Action (SOA) in the Rural/ Community (TruBridge) installed base ●Platform sales in mid-size Health Systems / Medical Groups ●Evolve from T ech led, HITL to Autonomy through explainable AI for non-deterministic outcomes ●Execute Operating model Transformation in TruBridge RCM & Coding Businesses ●Realize Operating and SG&A Synergies ●Continue to institutionalize an outcome driven culture and operating model to enable outcome based deals ●Consolidated Leadership team leveraging complementary strengths and capabilities ●One Uniﬁed Culture based on intentional manifest of value behaviors 4 5 Awards and Recognition Best CFO & Finance Strategy Excellence Awards 2026 1. Excellence in Investor Relations (Organisational category) 2. Best CFO in Healthcare – Nithya Balasubramanian, Whole-time Director & Group CFO (Individual category) US Patent US 12,619,923 В2 for Engagement Learning Engine AI-driven “Awareness-Ability-Willingness” (AAW) behavioral modeling powers IKS Health’s patient access solutions including MyCareHub which enhance patient engagement and optimize patient scheduling. 2026 Dallas-Fort Worth Titan 100 Titan CEO - Sachin K. Gupta, Founder & Global CEO 6 Awards and Recognition American Medical Group Association (AMGA) Distinguished Corporate Partner Award 2026 Axia Women’s Health IKS Health partnership for medical coding delivered $12 Million in annual cash impact with 96%+ coding accuracy and 37% lower coding related denials FE HR Awards 2026 Excellence in Onboarding & Role Enablement Legend Pre-visit Peri-visit In between visits Post-visit Optimized Scheduling Patient Financial Clearance Patient Engagement Hub Autonomous Coding Referral Order Management IKS ScribbleTM Pre-Visit Summary Billing and Denial Prevention Payment Posting and Denial Management Concurrent and Denovo Risk Coding Patient AR Management Care Management and UM Inbox Management IKS AssuRxTM IKS StacksTM In-acute settings Prospective Clinical Chart Reviews Clinical Documentation Solutions Clinical Coding And CDI Revenue Optimization Solutions Medico-legal Documentation Solutions Discharge Summary Automation Level 1 2 3 4 5 Fully Manual Fully Autonomous 7 IKS Health enables care transformation across the patient journey",
