      "text": "Solitaire Corporate Park Office: IndusInd Bank Limited, Building No.7, Ground floor, Solitaire Corporate Park, Andheri –Ghatkopar Link Road, Chakala Andheri (E), Mumbai – 400 093, India, Tel: (022) 66412442 Registered Office: 2401 Gen. Thimmayya Road, Pune 411001, India Contact us:(020) 2634 3201| Email us: reachus@indusind.com | Visit us:www.indusind.bank.in CIN: L65191PN1994PLC076333 August 5, 2026 National Stock Exchange of India Limited (Symbol: INDUSINDBK) BSE Limited (Scrip Code: 532187) Luxembourg Stock Exchange Madam / Dear Sir, Sub.: Notice of 32nd Annual General Meeting and the Integrated Annual Report for FY 2025-26 Ref.: Regulations 30 and 34 of the SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 This is in furtherance to our letter dated July 22, 2026, wherein the Bank had intimated regarding convening of 32 nd Annual General Meeting (“AGM”) of the Bank at 2.00 p.m. on Thursday, August 27, 2026, through Video Conference/Other Audio Visual Means (‘VC/OAVM”). In this regard, we enclose herewith the Notice of 32nd AGM and the Integrated Annual Report for FY 2025-26. The same is being sent today i.e. Wednesday, August 5, 2026, through electronic mode to those Members whose email addresses are registered with the Bank / Registrar & Share Transfer Agent, ‘MUFG Intime India Private Limited’ ( Erstwhile, ‘Link Intime India Private Limited’) / Depository Participant(s) as on Friday, July 24, 2026. The Notice and Integrated Annual Report are also available on the website of the Bank at: https://www.indusind.bank.in/in/en/investors/investor-landing.html Brief details of the business(es) proposed to be transacted at the AGM are enclosed as Annexure A. This is for your information and record. Yours faithfully, For IndusInd Bank Limited Anand Kumar Das Company Secretary Encl.: As above Solitaire Corporate Park Office: IndusInd Bank Limited, Building No.7, Ground floor, Solitaire Corporate Park, Andheri –Ghatkopar Link Road, Chakala Andheri (E), Mumbai – 400 093, India, Tel: (022) 66412442 Registered Office: 2401 Gen. Thimmayya Road, Pune 411001, India Contact us:(020) 2634 3201| Email us: reachus@indusind.com | Visit us:www.indusind.bank.in CIN: L65191PN1994PLC076333 Annexure A Brief details of the Business(es) proposed to be transacted at the 32nd AGM Sr No. Description Type of Resolution Ordinary Business 1. To receive, consider and adopt the Audited Financial Statements (Standalone and Consolidated) of the Bank for the Financial Year ended March 31, 2026, together with the Reports of the Board of Directors’ and Auditors’ thereon. Ordinary 2. To declare dividend at the rate of ₹1.50 per equity share of ₹10 each of the Bank, fully paid, for the Financial Year ended March 31, 2026. Ordinary 3. To re-appoint Mr. Sudip Basu (DIN: 09743986) as a Director who retires by rotation and being eligible has offered himself for re-appointment. Ordinary 4. To approve payment of remuneration of the Joint Statutory Auditors of the Bank for the Financial Year 2026-27. Ordinary Special Business 5. Issue of Long -Term Bonds / Debt Securities on Private Placement Basis. Special 6. Augmentation of capital through further issue or placement of securities including American Depository Receipts, Global Depository Receipts, Qualified Institutional Placement, etc. Special 7. Revision in the remuneration payable to Mr. Rajiv Anand (DIN: 02541753), Managing Director & Chief Executive Officer (MD & CEO) of the Bank with effect from April 1, 2026. Ordinary 8. Appointment of Mr. Ganesh Sankaran (DIN: 07580955) as an Executive Director (Wholetime Director) of the Bank and payment of remuneration. Ordinary 9. Appointment of Mr. Jagdeep Mallareddy (DIN: 07492539) as an Executive Director (Wholetime Director) of the Bank and payment of remuneration. Ordinary 10. Appointment of Ms. Mini Ipe (DIN: 07791184) as the Non - Executive Independent Director of the Bank. Special Integrated Annual Report 2025-26 EMPOWERING AMBITION. EXPANDING POSSIBILITY. Ambition is a powerful catalyst of progress. It fuels aspiration, unlocks opportunity, and creates momentum for sustained growth. As ambition evolves, it calls for solutions that are timely, relevant, and responsive to changing needs, creating new possibilities for growth and advancement. At IndusInd Bank, empowering ambition is central to the way we serve our customers. Strong relationships, deep financial expertise, digital capabilities, data intelligence, and AI strengthen every customer interaction. Decisions are faster, experiences are more intuitive, and solutions are tailored to deliver greater relevance and value. Every interaction reflects our commitment to serving with consistency, insight, and purpose. FY2026 reinforced this commitment. Consumer Banking, Corporate Banking, and Tr easury expanded their capabilities, digital transformation accelerated, and technology & AI became more deeply embedded across customer journeys and business operations. These advancements have enhanced the way we serve, enabling greater agility, deeper insights, and more meaningful outcomes. By empowering ambitions and expanding possibilities, we continue to strengthen our ability to support evolving customer aspirations and create opportunities for sustained growth. WHAT’SINSIDE About the Report02 Key Highlights18 Corporate Overview22 About IndusInd Bank24 Management Messages06 Message from the Chairman Message from the Managing Director & CEO Governance16 Board of Directors Leadership Team Business Overview26 Products and Client Coverage Key Market Differentiators Value Creation Model Operating Context Strategic Priorities Stakeholder Engagement Materiality Assessment The Capitals50 Financial Capital Manufactured Capital Intellectual Capital Hum an Capital Social and Relationship Capital Natural Capital Awards and Accolades Corporate Information MDA88 Management Discussion and Analysis Statutory Reports167 Director’s Report Corporate Governance Report 