      "text": "ISO CERTIFIED 9001:2015 Regd. Office Phone E-mail Website : W44, M.I.D.C. Phase II, Manpada Road, Dombivli (E) Dist Thane – 421203, Maharashtra. India. : 7045592703 / 7045592706 / 7498245178 / 8291098827 : shares@indoaminesltd.com : www.indoaminesltd.com CIN: L99999MH1992PLC070022 INDO AMINES LIMITED Date: 12th August, 2026 Subject: Revocation of Closure Directions issued by Gujarat Pollution Control Board Ref: Earlier Intimation dated July 21, 2026, pursuant to Regulation 30 of SEBI (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 (‘SEBI Listing Regulations’). Dear Sir/Madam, This is in continuation to our disclosure dated July 21, 2026, wherein the Company had intimated the receipt of Closure Directions issued by the Gujarat Pollution Control Board (“GPCB”) under Section 33A of the Water (Prevention and Control of Pollution) Act, 1974 (“Water Act”) and Section 31A of the Air (Prevention and Control of Pollution) Act, 1981 (“Air Act”), directing closure of the manufacturing operations at the Company’s plant located at Plot No. 1723, 1724 and 1746, Village Tundav, Tal. Savli, Dist. Vadodara – 392530, Gujarat. The Company has received Revocation Orders dated August 11, 2026, from the GPCB revoking the aforesaid Closure Directions issued under the Water Act and the Air Act, respectively, for a period of three months, subject to compliance with the conditions stipulated therein. The revocation follows an inspection of the Company’s plant conducted by the GPCB on July 31, 2026, wherein the GPCB observed various corrective and preventive measures undertaken by the Company in respect of the observations forming part of the Closure Directions and, accordingly, directed revocation thereof for the aforesaid period, subject to the specified conditions. The additional information pursuant to the Industry Standards Note on Regulation 30 of the SEBI Listing Regulations read with the SEBI Master Circular HO/49/14/14(7)2025-CFDPOD2/I/3762/2026 dated January 30, 2026, is provided under ‘Form A’. The requisite information as per Para A of Part A of Schedule III under Regulation 30 of the SEBI Listing Regulations is given below: To, Manager, Listing Department National Stock Exchange of India Ltd. Plot no. C/1G Block, Bandra-Kurla Complex, Bandra (East), Mumbai-400051 Symbol: INDOAMIN To, General Manager, Listing Department BSE Limited Phiroze Jeejeebhoy Towers, Dalal Street, Mumbai-400001 Script Code: 524648 ISO CERTIFIED 9001:2015 Regd. Office Phone E-mail Website : W44, M.I.D.C. Phase II, Manpada Road, Dombivli (E) Dist Thane – 421203, Maharashtra. India. : 7045592703 / 7045592706 / 7498245178 / 8291098827 : shares@indoaminesltd.com : www.indoaminesltd.com CIN: L99999MH1992PLC070022 INDO AMINES LIMITED Name of the Authority Gujarat Pollution Control Board (GPCB) Nature and details of the action(s) taken or order(s) passed The Company has received orders dated August 11, 2026 from the Gujarat Pollution Control Board (GPCB) revoking the Closure Directions issued under Section 33A of the Water Act and Section 31A of the Air Act in respect of the Company's manufacturing plant located at Plot No. 1723, 1724 and 1746, Village Tundav, Tal. Savli, Dist. Vadodara – 392530, Gujarat. The revocation of the Closure Directions is for a period of three months and is subject to compliance with the conditions stipulated by GPCB. Date of receipt of direction or order, including any ad-interim or interim orders, or any other communication from the authority August 11, 2026 Details of the violation(s)/ contravention(s) committed or alleged to be committed No fresh violation or contravention has been identified in the Revocation Orders. The disclosure is consequent to the receipt of the Revocation Orders issued by GPCB in respect of the Closure Directions earlier issued for the Company’s manufacturing plant located at Plot No. 1723, 1724 and 1746, Village Tundav, Tal. Savli, Dist. Vadodara – 392530, Gujarat. Impact on financial, operation or other activities of the listed entity, quantifiable in monetary terms to the extent possible Pursuant to the revocation orders issued by GPCB, the Closure Directions have been revoked for a period of three months. Accordingly, the Company is permitted to undertake its manufacturing operations at the said plant, subject to compliance with the conditions specified by GPCB. The Company does not envisage any material adverse impact on its financial or operational activities pursuant to the revocation of the Closure Directions, subject to continued compliance with the conditions stipulated by GPCB. The Company will continue to take all necessary corrective, preventive and compliance measures in accordance with the directions of GPCB. ISO CERTIFIED 9001:2015 Regd. Office Phone E-mail Website : W44, M.I.D.C. Phase II, Manpada Road, Dombivli (E) Dist Thane – 421203, Maharashtra. India. : 7045592703 / 7045592706 / 7498245178 / 8291098827 : shares@indoaminesltd.com : www.indoaminesltd.com CIN: L99999MH1992PLC070022 INDO AMINES LIMITED The Company will continue to monitor the matter and will make further disclosures to the Stock Exchanges as may be required under applicable laws. The manufacturing activities at all other manufacturing units of the Company will continue to remain operational. This is for your information and record. Thanking You. Yours truly, For Indo Amines Limited Tripti Sawant Company Secretary & Compliance Officer Mem. No: A39926 ISO CERTIFIED 9001:2015 Regd. Office Phone E-mail Website : W44, M.I.D.C. Phase II, Manpada Road, Dombivli (E) Dist Thane – 421203, Maharashtra. India. : 7045592703 / 7045592706 / 7498245178 / 8291098827 : shares@indoaminesltd.com : www.indoaminesltd.com CIN: L99999MH1992PLC070022 INDO AMINES LIMITED Date: 12th August, 2026 Dear Sir/ Madam, In respect of the captioned matter, I, the undersigned, state and declare that the information and details provided in Form A, in compliance with Regulation 30(13) of the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015, is true, correct and complete to the best of my knowledge and belief. This is for your information and records. Thanking You. Yours truly, For Indo Amines Limited Tripti Sawant Company Secretary & Compliance Officer Mem. No: A39926 To, Manager, Listing Department National Stock Exchange of India Ltd. Plot no. C/1G Block, Bandra-Kurla Complex, Bandra (East), Mumbai-400051 Symbol: INDOAMIN To, General Manager, Listing Department BSE Limited Phiroze Jeejeebhoy Towers, Dalal Street, Mumbai-400001 Script Code: 524648 ISO CERTIFIED 9001:2015 Regd. Office Phone E-mail Website : W44, M.I.D.C. Phase II, Manpada Road, Dombivli (E) Dist Thane – 421203, Maharashtra. India. : 7045592703 / 7045592706 / 7498245178 / 8291098827 : shares@indoaminesltd.com : www.indoaminesltd.com CIN: L99999MH1992PLC070022 INDO AMINES LIMITED FORM - A Disclosure pursuant to Regulation 30(13) by Indo Amines Limited regarding receipt of communication from regulatory, statutory, enforcement or judicial authority under the Securities and Exchange Board of India (Listing Obligations and Disclosure Requirements) Regulations, 2015 Sr. No Particulars Details 1. Name of the Listed Company Indo Amines Limited 2. Type of communication received Revocation of Closure Directions issued under Section 33A of the Water (Prevention and Control of Pollution) Act, 1974 and Section 31A of the Air (Prevention and Control of Pollution) Act, 1981. 3. Date of receipt of communication August 11, 2026 4. Authority from whom communication received Gujarat Pollution Control Board (GPCB) 5. Brief summary of the material contents of the communication received, including reasons for receipt of the communication The Company had submitted applications and undertaken corrective and preventive measures pursuant to the Closure Directions issued by GPCB on July 21, 2026. Pursuant thereto, authorised officers of GPCB inspected the Company's plant on July 31, 2026, and observed various corrective measures undertaken by the Company. Based on the aforesaid compliance, GPCB has issued orders dated August 11, 2026, revoking the Closure Directions issued under the Water Act and Air Act for a period of three months, subject to specified conditions. 6. Period for which communication would be applicable, if stated The revocation of the Closure Directions is applicable for a period of three months from the date of the respective orders, subject to the conditions stipulated therein. 7. Expected financial implications on the listed company, if any The revocation of the Closure Directions enables the Company to undertake manufacturing operations at the said plant, subject to compliance with the conditions stipulated by GPCB. The Company does not envisage any material adverse financial impact arising from the revocation order, subject to continued compliance with the ISO CERTIFIED 9001:2015 Regd. Office Phone E-mail Website : W44, M.I.D.C. Phase II, Manpada Road, Dombivli (E) Dist Thane – 421203, Maharashtra. India. : 7045592703 / 7045592706 / 7498245178 / 8291098827 : shares@indoaminesltd.com : www.indoaminesltd.com CIN: L99999MH1992PLC070022 INDO AMINES LIMITED conditions prescribed by GPCB. 8. Details of any aberrations/ noncompliances identified by the authority in the communication No fresh aberrations or non-compliances have been identified in the Revocation Orders. The disclosure is consequent to the receipt of the Revocation Orders issued by GPCB in respect of the Closure Directions earlier issued for the Company’s manufacturing plant located at Plot No. 1723, 1724 and 1746, Village Tundav, Tal. Savli, Dist. Vadodara – 392530, Gujarat. 9. Details of any penalty or restriction or sanction imposed pursuant to the communication. The Closure Directions issued earlier by GPCB have been revoked for a period of three months, subject to compliance with the conditions stipulated in the revocation orders. The Company has submitted a bank guarantee of ₹5,00,000/- valid up to September 30, 2027, and has paid interim Environment Damage Compensation of ₹5,70,000/- to GPCB in respect of the Water Act Closure Direction. 10. Action(s) taken by listed company with respect to the communication The Company will continue to comply with the conditions stipulated in the revocation orders and undertake necessary corrective, preventive and environmental compliance measures. 11. Any other relevant information -",
